      "body": "# Change type\n\n- [x] Computation\n- [x] Documentation\n\n## Exact change\n\nAn accepted `NO_GO` scientific result can still leave the original Task's process obligations unresolved. Add `RESULT_ACCEPTED_TASK_OPEN_CONTINUATION` and the nonterminal runtime state `ACCEPTED_RESULT_TASK_INCOMPLETE` so this evidence can be retained without declaring the Task complete or making it claimable.\n\nThe route requires ACCEPTED/NONE, unchanged raw/view NO_GO, explicit process UNKNOWN and residual obligations, all six existing gates, and current Driver/session/exact-review-set/CAS authority. The immutable scientific DR's complete report binds the full interface and exact scope quotation; an authorized successor uses its own DA/session. Current Source membership is verified in Git and no-Git snapshots; historical locators remain provenance only.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe JSON evidence capsule in this branch preserves the exact author manifest, independent final code review, original rejected v1 finding, attack replay, test logs, and bilingual review. Independent v2 review passed with no must-fix findings; the original interface-substitution attack was rejected. The real scoped scientific report was separately published at Source `803cc74beea23a60b33bc33ed0443054b73bb3e8`; this PR adds no scientific acceptance.\n\n## Claim status\n\nThis is an isolated, reviewed control candidate. Source main and the deployed MCP code are unchanged. **Keep this draft until coordinated Native public-contract/ref updates and the real `reviewed_python_blobs` approval are complete. Do not merge Source alone.** Verify deployed support and Source synchronization before sending the new decision. No Native DR/new decision, Task completion, parent closure, Foundation or tool promotion is claimed.\n\n## Shared theorem/tool surface\n\nShared-surface delta: N/A. This changes control flow and existing tools only; it adds or removes no repository tool, Lean root import, theorem, or reusable mathematical asset.\n\n- [x] Shared-surface applicability checked.\n- [x] No root Lean import changes.\n- [x] No added/removed `tools/*.py` files.\n\n## Bilingual parity\n\n- [x] Both new canonical prose versions and their registry entry are included.\n- [x] Independent full-text semantic parity review passed; English preserves the reviewed original bytes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Frozen v2: 13 fresh-process scenarios, including 20 binding rejection variants; 42 existing control regressions passed.\n- Independent replay: exact v1 attack rejected; legitimate successor, current no-Git snapshot/Source advance, and binding negative cases passed.\n- Actual published branch: all 13 files / 506,543 bytes fully matched SHA256 and Git blobs; exact changed-set check passed.\n- `python tools/check_bilingual_pairs.py --base 721f969b70fcaef86cd2dc4c4e8b60dfd154a373`: PASS, 135 pairs.\n- Common-surface checker using the supported `research_control_bootstrap.install(Path.cwd())` entry: PASS (20 Lean imports, 29 repo tools). Direct unbootstrapped file invocation encounters the existing module-import-path issue.\n- `git -c core.whitespace=cr-at-eol diff --check`: PASS; existing CRLF contract encoding preserved.\n",
